oman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campaigns_of_Nader_Shah","c":3},{"y":1732,"t":"gain","x":"1732: the Treaty of Resht.","cp":"russian-empire","cpn":"Russian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Constantinople_(1724)","c":2},{"y":1735,"t":"gain","x":"1735: the Treaty of Ganja returns the rest.","cp":"russian-empire","cpn":"Russian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Constantinople_(1724)","c":2},{"y":1735,"t":"gain","x":"1735: Iran recovers the Caucasus.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Constantinople_(1724)","c":2},{"y":1735,"t":"contest_end","x":"1735: the war of 1730-1735 ends (peace of 1735/1736).","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Constantinople_(1724)","c":2},{"y":1736,"t":"dissolve","x":"8 March 1736: Nader Shah is crowned and the Safavid state ends.","m":3,"cp":"afsharid-iran","cpn":"Afsharid Iran","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safavid_Iran","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Ottoman-Safavid War under Selim I (1505-1517)","from":1505,"to":1517,"outcome":"Ottoman victory at Chaldiran (1514); the Ottomans enter Tabriz but leave it, and annex Eastern Anatolia and parts of Mesopotamia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars"},{"name":"Ottoman-Safavid War (1532-1555)","from":1532,"to":1555,"outcome":"Ottoman victory: Tahmasp recognises Ottoman sovereignty in Mesopotamia and much of Kurdistan (Peace of Amasya, June 1555); eastern Georgia stays Safavid, western Georgia goes to the Turks.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars"},{"name":"Safavid-Uzbek wars of Tahmasp I (1524-1528)","from":1524,"to":1528,"outcome":"The Uzbeks under Ubayd Allah Khan overrun the Khorasan borderlands (1524) and Astarabad and Tus (1528); Tahmasp wins at Jam in 1528.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tahmasp_I"},{"name":"Ottoman-Safavid War (1578-1590)","from":1578,"to":1590,"outcome":"Ottoman victory: the Treaty of Constantinople (1590) cedes Azerbaijan, Karabagh, Shirvan, Dagestan, parts of Georgia, Lorestan, Kurdistan and Tabriz.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbas_I_of_Persia"},{"name":"Safavid-Uzbek wars of Abbas I (1589-1602)","from":1589,"to":1602,"outcome":"The Uzbeks take Herat (1589); Abbas retakes Mashhad (April 1598) and Herat, reaches Balkh in 1599 and loses it again in 1602.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbas_I_of_Persia"},{"name":"Ottoman-Safavid War (1603-1618)","from":1603,"to":1618,"outcome":"Persian victory: the Treaty of Nasuh Pasha (20 November 1612) 'recognized Persian victories and restored suzerainty over most of the Caucasus'; the second phase, 1616-1618, ended with an Ottoman army of 100,000 under Halil Pasha seizing Tabriz and being…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman%E2%80%93Safavid_War_(1603%E2%80%931618)"},{"name":"Safavid suppression of the Georgian revolt (1614-1616)","from":1614,"to":1616,"outcome":"Iranian armies invaded Kartli and Kakheti in March 1614 and suppressed the revolt of Luarsab II and Teimuraz I; Abbas deported 30,000 Kakhetian peasants and in 1619 made Simon II the puppet ruler of Kartli.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbas_I_of_Persia"},{"name":"Safavid-Portuguese conflict in the Gulf (1602-1622)","from":1602,"to":1622,"outcome":"The Portuguese lose Bahrain (1602) and, with four English ships helping Abbas, Hormuz (1622).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safavid_Iran"},{"name":"Ottoman-Safavid War (1623-1639)","from":1623,"to":1639,"outcome":"Ottoman victory: Murad IV takes Baghdad (December 1638) and the Treaty of Zuhab (17 May 1639) cedes Iraq for good and fixes the Turkey-Iran and Iraq-Iran border.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman%E2%80%93Safavid_War_(1623%E2%80%931639)"},{"name":"Mughal-Safavid war (1649-1653)","from":1648,"to":1653,"outcome":"Safavid victory: Kandahar falls again to the Safavids (infobox) and on 29 September 1653 the Mughals 'finally gave up all attempts to recover Kandahar'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mughal%E2%80%93Safavid_war_(1649%E2%80%931653)"},{"name":"Hotaki invasion of Persia (1722-1729)","from":1722,"to":1729,"outcome":"Gulnabad (8 March 1722), siege of Isfahan, abdication of Soltan Hoseyn (23 October 1722); the Hotaki are beaten at Damghan in autumn 1729.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hotak_dynasty"},{"name":"Russian and Ottoman partition of the Safavid periphery (1722-1724)","from":1722,"to":1724,"outcome":"Peter the Great declares war in June 1722; the Treaty of Saint Petersburg (1723) cedes the Caspian provinces to Russia; the Treaty of Constantinople (12 June 1724) divides the periphery between Russia and the Ottomans.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Constantinople_(1724)"},{"name":"Ottoman-Persian War (1730-1735)","from":1730,"to":1735,"outcome":"Persian victory: 'decisively returned all Ottoman annexed territories back to Iran'; with the Treaties of Resht (1732) and Ganja (1735) the Russian gains also return.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Constantinople_(1724)"}],"certainty":[{"from":1501,"to":1638,"level":"soft","note":"Approximate frontiers in the east, the Gulf, Georgia and the Ottoman marches; the Peace of Amasya (1555) and the Treaty of Constantinople (1590) name lands but no lines."},{"from":1639,"to":1721,"level":"sharp","note":"Sharp on the Ottoman frontier from the Treaty of Zuhab (1639), 'the western border of Iran with Iraq and Turkey' to this day; the eastern marches (Kandahar, Herat, Baluchistan) and the Gulf coast stay soft."},{"from":1722,"to":1736,"level":"soft","note":"Collapse, occupation and partition: treaty lines of 1723, 1724, 1732 and 1735 exist, but the territory of the exiled court is not located by the pages opened."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safavid_dynasty","title":"Safavid dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safavid_Iran","title":"Safavid Iran"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman%E2%80%93Persian_Wars","title":"Ottoman-Persian Wars"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismail_I","title":"Ismail I"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tahmasp_I","title":"Tahmasp I"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbas_I_of_Persia","title":"Abbas I of Persia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman%E2%80%93Safavid_War_(1623%E2%80%931639)","title":"Ottoman-Safavid War (1623-1639)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hotak_dynasty","title":"Hotak dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tahmasp_II","title":"Tahmasp II"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Constantinople_(1724)","title":"Treaty of Constantinople (1724)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Campaigns_of_Nader_Shah","title":"Campaigns of Nader Shah"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akbar","title":"Akbar"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mughal%E2%80%93Safavid_war_(1649%E2%80%931653)","title":"Mughal-Safavid war (1649-1653)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mughal%E2%80%93Persian_wars","title":"Mughal-Persian wars"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottoman%E2%80%93Safavid_War_(1603%E2%80%931618)","title":"Ottoman-Safavid War (1603-1618)"}]}